rror", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 47364, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I could not complete the order as a single purchase order. The docks were ordered, but the monitors were not.\n\n**Current state:**\n- **PO0001** (primary vendor, ship to HQ, status `partially_placed`): 3 \u00d7 DK-200 (new), $567. This is the only order on the books.\n- **MN-27 monitors (3 \u00d7 $329 = $987): not ordered.** The original request failed after the first line item with an upstream fulfilment error. The retry with the same idempotency key was refused because that request already failed partway, so I did not place a second attempt.\n\nThe DK-200 was in stock as new equipment, so the DK-210 fallback was not needed. The full order would have been $1,554, under the $2,500 approval threshold.\n\n**Options (I have not taken any of these):**\n1. **Order the monitors separately** via the primary vendor (3 \u00d7 MN-27, ship to HQ, about $987). This gives you all the equipment, but across two POs rather than one.\n2. **Cancel PO0001 (refunds the $567)** and place one combined order for 3 \u00d7 DK-200 and 3 \u00d7 MN-27 under a new key. This meets the single-PO requirement, but the upstream error could recur.\n3. **Try the secondary vendor** (`place_order_vendor_b`) for the monitors, which would also split the order across two vendors.\n\nWhich would you like? I can also check the order list again first to see whether the upstream issue has cleared.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RPRc72AL95E7CfYRp2g9Pz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"category": "dock"}, "name": "search_catalog", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012Je1dqGsDGtpGD4H3UXF6v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"category": "monitor"}, "name": "search_catalog", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use",